What does this print?

```python
class Pos:
    def __set_name__(self, owner, name):
        self.n = name
    def __get__(self, obj, objtype=None):
        return self if obj is None else self.v
    def __set__(self, obj, v):
        self.v = v

class M:
    x = Pos()

a, b = M(), M()
a.x = 1
b.x = 2
print(a.x, b.x)
```

What does this print?

```python
class A:
    @property
    def x(self):
        return "prop"

class B:
    def x(self):
        return "meth"

a, b = A(), B()
a.__dict__["x"] = "inst"
b.__dict__["x"] = "inst"
print(a.x)
print(b.x)
```

